UID:3FPz3cOTDPJ5gohF8ND07
SUMMARY:Optimizing the Building Enclosure Envelope CE Event
DTSTAMP:20260821T033712Z
DTSTART:20260916T163000Z
DESCRIPTION:Building Enclosure Council of Houston Presents:                
	           \nOptimizing the Building Enclosure Envelope \nGenerative Desig
	n Strategies for Early-Stage Architectural Performance \nPresenter: Joe Fo
	ng\, LEED AP \nDiscover how Autodesk Forma and Generative Design are trans
	forming the architectural workflow from early concept to team collaboratio
	n. In this session\, you’ll learn how to rapidly generate performance-base
	d building massings tailored to site constraints\, perform comprehensive s
	ite analyses early in the design phase\, and streamline team coordination.
	 Step into a unified\, shared workspace where design options can be evalua
	ted\, compared\, and refined in real time. \nAIA CE Credit: 1.0 LU \nSched
	ule: \n\n4:30pm – Check-in\n5:00pm – Presentation\n\nAdditional Informatio
	n: \n\nBeer & Wine Available\nParking is not included\nA minimum of 3 busi
	ness days’ notice is required to receive a full refund if you need to canc
	el your reservation.\n\n  \nTHANK YOU TO OUR UNDERWRITER SPONSOR! \n\nhttp
	s://architecturehouston.org/event/bec-houston-lunch-learn-3/\n\nFrom AIA H
	ouston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/bec-houston-lunch-learn-3/
